# City in a Bottle's second ability: "Players can't cast spells or play lands with a name originally printed in the Arabian
# Nights expansion" (CR 101.2, 601.3, 305.1). With it on the battlefield, its controller can't cast Kird Ape with an untapped
# Mox Ruby to pay for it, nor play Desert as the turn's land, though a Mox (not an Arabian Nights name) is cast and an Island
# played; on the next turn its opponent can't cast Camel off an untapped Mox Pearl nor play Oasis, and plays a Plains -
# and can't cast a second City in a Bottle off the Mox and the Plains either, its own name being an Arabian Nights one.
# No Arabian Nights permanent is on the battlefield, so its triggered ability does nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
City in a Bottle
Kird Ape
Desert
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Camel
Oasis
Plains
City in a Bottle
Island
Island
Island x20

